window.FWN_YOU_PROMISED_TO_BE_AN_IDLE_SON_IN_LAW_HOW_COULD_YOU_BECOME_A_LAND_IMMORTAL_CHAPTERS=(window.FWN_YOU_PROMISED_TO_BE_AN_IDLE_SON_IN_LAW_HOW_COULD_YOU_BECOME_A_LAND_IMMORTAL_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":601,"title":"Chapter 601 - 338: Only Advance, No Retreat","paragraphs":["By the time the Holy Emperor’s decree arrived in Shu State, it was already the twenty-ninth day of the ninth month.","Only one day remained until the Annual Examination.","Tomorrow, the scholars from the Prefecture City and surrounding counties and towns would all gather at the examination grounds—a large courtyard located between the Governor’s Office and the Prefectural Magistrate’s Office.","The examination would last for two days. They would enter at 5:00 AM, the exam would begin at 1:00 PM, and it would end at Noon on the second day.","Originally, Ma Shuhan, the Academic Administrator Officer of Shu State, had scheduled the Annual Examination for the twenty-eighth, but for some unspeakable reason, he had postponed it by two days. The scholars in the Prefecture City were not merely understanding or supportive of this change; they simply had no time to pay attention to it.","The reasons behind Liu Hong’s death had already spread far and wide: colluding with the enemy and betraying the country, manipulating grain prices, attempting to spread a plague, and so on. Each and every one of his crimes was posted on the notice board outside the Governor’s Office.","Listed alongside him were the crimes of those who had been taken away by the Imprisonment Department. Ye Jingxiao, the Vice Inspector General of the Inspectorate Office, had colluded with Lin’s Grain Store to frame loyal officials. Mr. Lingchuan from Guiyun Academy had secretly sold ironware to Poshisu Country on behalf of Commander-in-Chief Zhu Hao. Sun Wutong of the Sun Family had also played his part...","Except for a few individuals who were sentenced to exile, the rest, such as Ye Jingxiao and Zhu Lingchuan, were to be escorted to the Capital Prefecture to await execution after autumn.","As soon as these matters came to light, they caused an uproar throughout Shu State. The commoners cursed them incessantly. Although the soaring grain prices in the Prefecture City had not resulted in mass starvation, the people would never forget the panic of those days. This was true for everyone, whether they had managed to buy grain or not.","\"I originally thought that bastard Liu Hong was a good official, but I didn’t expect him to be so despicable behind the scenes.\"","\"To think I was actually grateful to him for opening the granaries, stabilizing grain prices, and providing disaster relief. Turns out none of that was his true intention.\"","\"Now I finally see clearly. In this Shu State, the only ones who truly treat us commoners well are the Xiao Family.\"","\"If Marquis Xiao hadn’t been unable to stand it anymore and confronted Liu Hong, the grain prices would still be sky-high. Many people would have definitely died back then.\"","\"Don’t forget, it was also Marquis Xiao who discovered the plague first and ordered the Government Office and Physicians to investigate inside and outside the Prefecture City overnight.\"","\"Marquis Xiao and the Xiao Family have protected Shu State for years. We... alas, we truly owe the old man an apology.\"","\"There’s also General Jinghong. The Commander-in-Chief who tried to flee this time was killed by her...\"","The common people on the streets held deep grudges against Liu Hong and the others, and the scholars were no exception. Most likely, the more they thought back on all the things they had done to try and save Mr. Lingchuan, the more ashamed they felt, prompting them to write articles cursing the traitors.","Sayings like \"you may know a person’s face, but not their heart\" were spread countless times. Even a few teachers at Guiyun Academy had voiced their criticisms of Zhu Lingchuan.","However, with the Annual Examination approaching, Mr. Yue Ming, Mr. Zhuo Ying, and others could only try to find ways to force the many scholars to focus. But clearly, it was of little effect.","\"Dean, just let them be.","\"The crimes Liu Gongmo committed this time are truly too massive. Even I want to curse him a few times.\"","Mr. Yue Ming naturally understood this reasoning. He sighed and said, \"Don’t you join in and add to the chaos.\"","Mr. Zhuo Ying raised an eyebrow. \"Adding to the chaos? Isn’t there enough already right now?","\"Before the Holy Emperor’s decree arrives, the Governor’s Office is completely leaderless. Yang Ye alone is already finding it more than he can handle.","\"The situation at the Inspectorate Office is slightly better, but I heard the Capital Commandery has been deeply affected.","\"Although the commoners over in Guangyuan County haven’t made many moves, those Noble Families have caused quite a few disturbances. They are mostly people in the same boat as Zhu Hao.","\"Salt, tea, water transport, carriages, and so on... the Capital Commandery is raiding one or two large clans almost every day. Some are killed, while others are exiled.\"","At this point, he pointed toward the Xiao Family with feigned mystery and said, \"I heard from people over in Guangyuan that Commander Li is making such moves because of Xiao Jinghong.\"","Mr. Yue Ming frowned slightly. \"Xiao Jinghong?\"","After thinking for a moment, his brow smoothed out. \"It must be that after she killed Zhu Hao last time, she heavily pressured the Capital Commandery.\"","Mr. Zhuo Ying smiled and nodded. \"Although that girl is a woman, she acts decisively and without hesitation. She has a bit of Xiao Fengchun’s flair.","\"On the other hand, Marquis Xiao... Dean, have you heard about the Xiao Family’s recent moves?","\"You should know a bit, seeing as you and Marquis Xiao are considered bosom friends.\"","Hearing this, Mr. Yue Ming glared at him. \"I am not familiar with him!\"","However, he had indeed heard about the Xiao Family’s recent situation. Ever since Liu Hong’s death, people from several families in the Prefecture City had flocked to visit the Xiao Family, all bringing copious amounts of gifts.","Take the Wan Family, for example. Not only did they gift the Xiao Family medicinal ingredients from their Medicine Hall, but they also brought ten thousand silver coins. The other few families did the same. It was as if the previous attacks the Xiao Family had endured from the various Noble Families of Shu State had never happened.","After a moment of silence, Mr. Yue Ming spoke. \"Liu Hong is dead, and the Jing State Liu Family behind him has also fallen. Anyone with a discerning eye can see that this was the work of the Xiao Family.","\"At this time, their visits to the Xiao Family are nothing more than an attempt to mend relations with them.\"","Mr. Zhuo Ying sneered. \"A bunch of fence-sitters. Since they weren’t implicated by Liu Hong, they will sooner or later be settled by Marquis Xiao.\" He toyed with the teacup in his hand and changed the subject. \"However, with Qingzhou not coming to the academy these past few days, I’m still a bit unaccustomed to it.\"","\"With the Annual Examination approaching, it’s normal for Qingzhou to study harder,\" Mr. Yue Ming said.","\"With Qingzhou’s knowledge, if he can’t make it into the top three of the Annual Examination, who else could?\"","\"Hard to say.\" Mr. Yue Ming thought of the Academic Administrator Officer who hadn’t been affected by Liu Hong, and said with a slight sigh, \"If Ma Shuhan doesn’t play any tricks, even if Qingzhou doesn’t make the top three, he will still rank among the best. I’m just afraid that Ma Shuhan won’t act according to common sense.\"","Mr. Zhuo Ying snorted. \"Would he dare?","\"Previously, he had Liu Hong backing him up. Now that Liu Hong is dead and the Governor’s Office is controlled by Lord Yang, how could he still be allowed to act recklessly?\""]},{"number":602,"title":"Chapter 602 - 338: Only Advance, No Retreat","paragraphs":["\"I hope so...\"","Just as Mr. Yue Ming was agonizing over how to pacify the academy students and get them to focus on preparing for the Annual Examination, the sound of footsteps came from outside the door.","Ma Guan’s figure appeared shortly after. He panted, \"De-Dean, Mr. Zhuo Ying, the Holy Emperor’s decree has arrived in Shu State.\"","\"Quick, tell us.\"","\"Eunuch Feng, the Chief Eunuch who arrived a few days ago, went to the Governor’s Office first.\" Ma Guan caught his breath, calmed down, and said, \"Lord Yang is temporarily acting as the Governor.\"","Mr. Yue Ming and Mr. Zhuo Ying exchanged a glance, visible relief washing over their faces.","\"Dean, with Elder Yang overseeing the Governor’s Office, the Annual Examination should proceed much more smoothly.\"","Mr. Yue Ming nodded slightly. \"If Ma Shuhan dares to act arbitrarily, I will naturally go and reason with him.\"","He had previously approached Yang Ye when Ma Shuhan invited him to serve as a deputy examiner; their personal relationship was decent. He then looked at Ma Guan. \"Where did Eunuch Feng go after leaving the Governor’s Office?\"","Ma Guan shook his head. \"Dean, Eunuch Feng is still at the Governor’s Office at this moment.\"","\"Oh?\"","\"Aside from Lord Yang, another person at the Governor’s Office received a reward from the Holy Emperor. It is the Golden Imperial Top Scholar, Chen Yunfan.","\"It’s said that he discovered Commander Zhu Hao’s iron trade with Poshisu Country and handed the evidence of his crimes to Inspector General Tang Zixing.","\"There’s also Lv Jiunan...\" Ma Guan said with a strange expression. \"For some unknown reason, the Holy Emperor’s decree stated that Assistant Governor Chen killed Lv Jiunan.\"","Mr. Yue Ming naturally had heard of Lv Jiunan’s name. He recalled, \"If I remember correctly, rumor has it that Lv Jiunan was killed by ’Dragon Tiger’ Liu Wu.\" He looked at Mr. Zhuo Ying. \"Is that right?\"","Mr. Zhuo Ying nodded and pondered for a moment. \"Could it be that Chen Yunfan is actually the famous Liu Wu of Shu State?\"","\"Him?\"","\"It is somewhat possible...\"","What absolute nonsense!","Chen Yunfan, currently at the Governor’s Office, truly couldn’t clear his name even if he had a hundred mouths.","Previously, he only thought that claiming credit with Lv Jiunan’s corpse would earn him Chen Yi’s mockery, but he had forgotten another crucial detail.","\"Dragon Tiger\" Liu Wu was hidden too deeply!","Now, not only did outsiders suspect he was Liu Wu, but even people inside the Governor’s Office shared the same thought. Li Huai’gu was one of them.","After Feng Erbao and the others left the Governor’s Office to head to the Xiao Family, Li Huai’gu came knocking. He looked Chen Yunfan up and down, cupped his fists, and said, \"Pardon my disrespect. I never expected Lord Assistant Governor to possess such profound Martial Arts.\"","Chen Yunfan rolled his eyes and tossed aside the imperial decree in his hand. \"Get lost, get lost... Stop bringing up things I don’t want to hear.","\"Anyone with eyes can see that this Assistant Governor couldn’t possibly be that ’Dragon Tiger’. Only idiots would think otherwise.\"","Li Huai’gu smiled and asked, \"Then why did the imperial decree state that you killed Lv Jiunan?\"","\"I...\" Chen Yunfan leaned back in his chair, waving his hand weakly. \"Forget it, forget it. Just treat me as that dog-fart Liu Wu.\"","He couldn’t exactly admit that he had merely picked up Lv Jiunan’s corpse. Saying that wouldn’t just strip him of all dignity; even the Holy Emperor would have to punish him for the crime of deceiving the sovereign.","Seeing this, Li Huai’gu sat down opposite him. He could mostly tell that there was a hidden story behind all this. After thinking for a moment, a hint of confusion appeared on his face. \"Logically speaking, since Brother Yunfan achieved such a great merit, the reward should have been much larger.\"","\"Larger?\" Chen Yunfan said grumpily. \"Brother Huai’gu, do you want the Holy Emperor to confer me the title of Right Minister of the Governor’s Office right now? Or take over Zhu Hao’s vacancy?\"","Despite his words, he was also somewhat puzzled.","Previously, when Chen Yi handed Zhu Hao’s criminal evidence to him on behalf of the White Tiger Guard, he thought that merit would allow him to take another step forward. Even if he didn’t skip a grade to reach the Junior Third Grade, he should have at least reached the Senior Fourth Grade.","But the truth was, he only received a few words of praise from the Holy Emperor, along with some gold, silver, and jewels.","After chatting for a few more sentences, Li Huai’gu got up and left.","Chen Yunfan sat quietly in his chair, looking out the window at the bright sun with a complex expression on his face. \"Now I don’t even know how Brother Yi is going to mock me...\"","Damn it, this was all Lin Zhong’s fault for being a busybody.","...","The Xiao Family.","Inside Spring Lotus Garden.","Chen Yi had naturally heard about the events at the Governor’s Office, as well as the fact that Chen Yunfan took credit for Lv Jiunan’s corpse. He figured it must have been the doing of Lin Zhong, the Chen Family’s Guard Commander.","This was fine, too. Lv Jiunan’s corpse keeping space here was bound to turn into dirt anyway; he might as well use it to give Chen Yunfan some achievements.","Moreover, there was an unexpected bonus—the people of Shu State deducing that Chen Yunfan was \"Dragon Tiger\" Liu Wu fit perfectly with Chen Yi’s wishes. Previously, he had used his illness from the plague poison to completely clear his own name. Now, with this incident involving Chen Yunfan, he guessed that no one would associate \"Liu Wu\" with him anymore.","Laughing it off, Chen Yi shifted his attention to the Qingjing Residence in the middle courtyard.","\"...Your merits and faults balance out, and you are fined three years of your salary. Respect this!\"","\"Xiao Yuan thanks the Holy Emperor for his grace.\"","\"Marquis Xiao, the Holy Emperor also asked me to pass a message to you.\"","\"Please speak, Eunuch Feng.\"","\"The Holy Emperor said that from now on, you can only advance and never retreat; otherwise, if chaos erupts in Shu State, you alone will be held responsible.\"","\"Please help me thank the Holy Emperor, Eunuch...\"","Hearing this, Chen Yi circulated the Black Tortoise Concealment Technique, drawing in his aura to prevent any leakage. He flipped through the ancient text in his hand, a smile curving his lips.","It was exactly as he had thought.","The current Holy Emperor didn’t reprimand the Old Master too harshly, merely fining him some salary to gloss over the matter. However, that oral decree was rather interesting.","He thought, \"The current Holy Emperor’s gaze must have been on Shu State this whole time. He is well aware of the Old Master’s recent actions.","\"Instead, the Old Master has become somewhat like a frightened bird, putting all his effort into restoring the Xiao Family’s prestige.\"","This wasn’t hard to deduce.","If the current Holy Emperor had wanted to use thunderous methods against the Xiao Family, he wouldn’t have let him and Chen Yunfan come to Shu State. He wouldn’t have done it before, and now that the Xiao Family’s situation was improving, he certainly wouldn’t do it now.","He estimated that...","The chessboard in Chen Yi’s mind shifted slightly. Several chess pieces hopped around, and as the game changed, his brows furrowed slightly.","\"Chen Yunfan has enough merit on his end, only lacking some seniority. Once the new year passes, the Capital Prefecture will issue a new decree for him,\" he analyzed. \"So... am I next?\"","Right now, the chessboard of Shu State was already gaining momentum, at least for Chen Yunfan. If Chen Yi was the Chess Master who laid out the plans, he would definitely push the board simultaneously to reach the endgame. In other words, this \"Fledgling\" had to accomplish something within the Xiao Family.","\"It seems this son-in-law will also have to make a move after the Annual Examination,\" he pondered.","Chen Yi thought about getting up to stretch his muscles. Just as he was about to tidy up the study, a shout came from outside the courtyard.","\"Brother-in-law, I’m back, brother-in-law...\"","Following closely were fits of RING RING RING sounds.","Chen Yi looked towards the sound and saw Pei Guanli bouncing and skipping her way over. Her tender white bare feet stepped on the bluestone slabs without leaving a single footprint, and the large bell on her chest bobbed up and down, swaying back and forth.","She first saw Xiaodie sweeping outside the wooden building and chuckled, \"Sister Xiaodie, where is my brother-in-law?\"","Xiaodie responded and smiled, \"The young master is in the study reading. The Annual Examination is tomorrow, don’t you...\"","Don’t you what? She couldn’t even finish her sentence.","Pei Guanli bypassed her and headed straight for the study, shouting for her brother-in-law.","Xiaodie scrambled to keep up behind her. \"Miss Pei, you, you shouldn’t disturb the young master’s reading.\"","\"It’s fine, it won’t get in the way. I’m just looking for...\" As Pei Guanli spoke, she arrived at the study. With one glance, she spotted Chen Yi standing at the desk, and a look of joy couldn’t help but appear on her face. \"Brother-in-law! I’m back!\"","Pei Guanli kicked off the ground and flew forward.","Chen Yi looked helpless. He calmly stepped sideways to dodge, grabbed her with a clever technique, and said, \"I’m not deaf, nor am I blind.\"","Pei Guanli held his hand and giggled, her eyes filled entirely with his reflection. But after laughing for a bit, she then pouted and grumbled, \"You say that, but brother-in-law promised me before that you’d pick me up once you were done with your work. In the end, I waited a long time and didn’t see you come.\"","Chen Yi signaled for Xiaodie to prepare lunch while casting a sidelong glance at Pei Guanli. \"How come I heard that you were in closed-door Cultivation?\"","Pei Guanli rolled her eyes twice, her lips curling up naturally. She pulled him and stammered, \"It’s all Third Granduncle’s fault. He insisted on teaching me some Witchcraft and Gu Skill, hehe...\"","Seeing Xiaodie walk far away, Chen Yi brushed Pei Guanli aside, sat down on a chair, and asked with a smile, \"Did your brother and the others go back?\"","Pei Guanli leaned against his side, tilted her face up to look at him, and nodded. \"Ah Ma sent a letter telling them to return.\"","\"So urgently? Did something happen with the Mountain Race?\"","\"Not in the tribe. Brother said that the Wu Mountain Mutual Market is about to be completed, so Ah Ma asked him to go back and prepare mountain goods.\"","Chen Yi realized. Before Xiao Jinghong left, she had mentioned the matter of the Mutual Market; now, it was finally nearing completion. This could be considered one of the few pieces of good news for the Xiao Family recently.","Pei Guanli didn’t think about all that. She chirped continuously, chattering about the things she had heard during her closed-door Cultivation.","\"Brother-in-law, did you know that something major is about to happen in the Jianghu?\""]},{"number":603,"title":"Chapter 603 - 339: I Am Also a Fool!","paragraphs":["A major event in the Jianghu.","Chen Yi naturally knew about it. It was nothing more than the duel between Immortal Bai and some swordsman.","\"What’s the matter?\" Chen Yi asked.","Seeing him looking over, Pei Guanli lowered her voice and said, \"Ah Ma said in her letter that Immortal Bai, the most powerful person in the Jianghu, is going to duel someone in the upper reaches of the Chishui River.\"","\"Duel who?\"","\"Monarch Xue Jian, Lone Immortal Ye.\"","Chen Yi raised an eyebrow. \"This person...\"","\"Brother-in-law, you also know Monarch Xue Jian? My brother and Third Granduncle both said he is the most powerful swordsman after Sword Master Li Wudang.\"","\"...Never heard of him.\"","\"He—\" Pei Guanli’s joyful smile faltered. \"You’ve never heard of him, brother-in-law?\"","Chen Yi smiled and nodded. \"I really don’t know him.\"","These past few days, his mind had been focused on solving the Xiao family’s troubles. The Jianghu anecdotes he occasionally heard were only fragmented and incomplete. Like the reclusive Immortal Bai, as well as his disciple Shui Hetong. Xiao Jinghong’s master, Sword Master Li Wudang. Liu Lang’s master, Sword Ghost Chu Xiudao, and the Celestial Sect where Xie Tingyun and Shen Huatang were from. These great seniors of the Jianghu were mostly connected to the people around Chen Yi, so he had heard more about them. As for the other Jianghu People, he naturally had never heard of them and didn’t care much either.","\"Tell me, what’s the background of this Monarch Xue Jian, Lone Immortal Ye?\"","Pei Guanli’s expression immediately brightened. She began to chatter away about Lone Immortal Ye.","She originally didn’t know who Monarch Xue Jian was either. Fortunately, Pei Qian and the others had told her quite a bit before they left.","\"Alone on the snowy peak for nineteen springs,","Plum blossoms fall on shoulders untouched by dust.","Today I draw my sword for you,","Only to realize I, too, am a fool.","\"Monarch Xue Jian was originally a legitimate son of the Ye family in Ji State. He was born with extraordinary talent.","\"It’s said that he started practicing Martial Arts at the age of six, and broke through to the Eighth Grade Realm by eight... Brother-in-law, what are you laughing at?\"","Chen Yi held back his laughter and waved his hand. \"I’m not laughing, I’m not. Go on.\"","Pei Guanli puffed out her cheeks, her round face full of indignation. \"I just had a mishap when practicing Martial Arts, but my Cultivation is also close to the Seventh Grade now.\"","However, thinking of Chen Yi’s current title of \"Dragon Tiger,\" she muttered a few words in resignation, saying things about how Third Granduncle had taught her a lot and that she would sooner or later reach the Middle Three Grades Realm.","Before Chen Yi could offer a few words of comfort, she continued, \"Third Granduncle said that Lone Immortal Ye reached the Sixth Grade at ten, and by fifteen, his Cultivation had already reached the Upper Fourth Grade. He was only one step away from breaking through to the Upper Three Grades Realm.","\"But right at that time...\"","When Lone Immortal Ye was sixteen, the Ye family committed a taboo. Not only did they offend a prominent family in Ji State, but they also accidentally killed a core disciple of the Gouchen Sect, bringing a great disaster upon the Ye family. First, the taverns the family relied on for their livelihood were ransacked. Then, the distant branch members died bizarre deaths one after another. And just as they were discussing whether to fight or seek peace, the people from the Gouchen Sect launched a night attack on their doorstep.","It was the Mid-Autumn Festival. There were exactly one hundred and forty-three people in the Ye family’s ancestral estate. Despite their desperate resistance, under the overwhelming power of the Gouchen Sect Leader, Lone Immortal Ye was the only one in the entire Ye family to escape alive.","\"After that, the Gouchen Sect relentlessly hunted Lone Immortal Ye down...\" Pei Guanli waved her fist, looking indignant herself. \"Fortunately, Lone Immortal Ye was strong enough. Not only did he escape, but he also took less than two years to advance his Cultivation to the First Grade Realm.\"","Chen Yi nodded in understanding. \"And then he successfully took his revenge?\"","Pei Guanli’s small face fell, and she shook her head. \"He only wiped out the entire Gouchen Sect. As for that prominent family, many of their people survived.\"","\"Oh?\"","\"According to my Third Granduncle, Lone Immortal Ye was saved by a woman while he was on the run. By sheer coincidence, she turned out to be the young lady of that very same prominent family.\"","\"So...\" Chen Yi raised an eyebrow. \"So he let that family off?\"","Pei Guanli hummed in agreement and pouted. \"When he went to seek revenge, he finally discovered that the woman belonged to that family, and...\" Shaking Chen Yi’s hand, she added, \"And by that time, they had already developed feelings for each other.\"","\"That family managed to survive thanks to that woman...\"","Chen Yi couldn’t help but laugh, likely finding such a story a bit clichéd.","Who knew Pei Guanli’s eyes would dart around as she asked him with a cheeky grin, \"Brother-in-law, what would you do if you were Lone Immortal Ye?\"","\"Me?\" Chen Yi thought about it seriously and shook his head. \"Me? I don’t know. But of course, it’s impossible for me to ever end up in that kind of situation.\"","Hadn’t he spent so much time on Cultivation just to protect himself and the people around him from harm? Given this, if he still managed to fall into a situation like Lone Immortal Ye’s, he might as well just bang his head against a brick wall.","\"What if... it was someone from the Mountain Race who killed the Chen family?\"","\"The Chen family? Then let them be killed.\"","Pei Guanli froze for a moment. \"Brother-in-law, you wouldn’t avenge the Chen family?\"","Chen Yi smiled and tapped her forehead. \"Because you are in the Mountain Race.\"","Pei Guanli immediately giggled, her face showing a rare blush. \"Brother-in-law, I’d never put you in a tough spot.","\"If anyone from the Mountain Race really is blind enough to cross you, I promise to plant a few Gu Insects in them and make them regret ever being born.\"","\"You’re one to talk,\" Chen Yi said. \"Did you forget about Poisoning Chen Yunfan last time?\"","\"Ah, geez...\"","Amidst the chatter and laughter, by the time Xiaodie came to announce that lunch was ready, Chen Yi had mostly understood what kind of person Lone Immortal Ye was.","After settling his grievances with the Le family—the prominent family in Ji State—Lone Immortal Ye lived a reclusive life, hiding away from the world. He stayed hidden for nineteen years. When he descended the mountain again, his Cultivation had reached the Grandmaster Realm, achieving Sword Dao Perfection. The last time news of Lone Immortal Ye spread was four years ago when he challenged Li Jin, a Grandmaster Realm swordsman in Ji State, and killed him in just ten sword strikes.","Chen Yi ate his lunch while silently calculating in his mind. If Lone Immortal Ye was capable of challenging Immortal Bai, his Cultivation and Sword Dao must have both ascended to a whole new level."]},{"number":604,"title":"Chapter 604 - 339: I Am Also a Fool!","paragraphs":["Either his Cultivation had reached the Great Grandmaster realm, or his Sword Dao had been honed to the Extreme Realm. Otherwise, even if Lone Immortal Ye was willing, Immortal Bai probably wouldn’t bother with him.","\"Great Grandmaster... Sword Dao Ultimate Realm...\"","Martial Arts Cultivation was divided from the Ninth Grade to the First Grade; above that were the realms of Grandmaster and Great Grandmaster. And the Technique Realm consisted of entry-level, Minor Success, Great Success, Perfection, and the Extreme Realm—where Skill Nears the Dao.","Reaching that realm earned one the respectful title of \"Land Immortal,\" meaning they had achieved \"Extreme Mortality.\"","However, even among those in that realm, there were differences in strength. Cultivation, Technique, Cultivation Technique, and talent—even the slightest variations could affect Heaven and Earth’s Spiritual Mechanism. For example, it was said that Immortal Bai had cultivated two Techniques to the Extreme Realm, which was why he was hailed as the number one person in Martial Arts.","At this thought, a smile naturally formed on Chen Yi’s face. He might fall short when it came to the Technique Realm, but in terms of sheer quantity, if he claimed to be second, who would dare claim to be first?","Of course, as long as he was given enough time, he would inevitably catch up.","After lunch, Chen Yi didn’t continue reading; instead, he planned to visit the Jishi Medicine Hall and the Hundred Herbs Hall. Since he had decided to turn from passive to active, he needed to make some preparations.","Seeing him change into a set of clean brocade clothes, Xiaodie couldn’t help but ask, \"Are you going out, Sir?\"","\"Yes. I’ve stayed in the manor for so many days, so I’m going out to stretch my legs.\"","\"B-but tomorrow is the Annual Examination.\"","Chen Yi adjusted his clothes, turned his head to look at her, and smiled. \"Studying requires a balance of tension and relaxation. Being strung too tight isn’t good.\"","Xiaodie nodded, half-understanding. \"I see...\"","Beside them, Pei Guanli started laughing, thinking that her brother-in-law was spouting nonsense again. However, seeing that Chen Yi was heading out, she trotted after him, clamoring that she wanted to go too.","Chen Yi thought for a moment and nodded in agreement. Pei Guanli then giggled and left the Spring Lotus Garden together with him.","Xiaodie watched them walk away, full of envy. Of course, she envied Pei Guanli.","In fact, during these past few days when Chen Yi had devoted all his attention to reading in the study, Xiaodie was the happiest person. Even though Chen Yi rarely needed her to serve him, she felt a sweet satisfaction in her heart and was brimming with energy. Boiling water, sweeping, doing laundry, serving tea, preparing meals, and so on—Xiaodie had grown accustomed to this routine and was used to staying by Chen Yi’s side.","Therefore, she really disliked being alone in the Spring Lotus Garden. Even though she would clean the inside and outside of the garden until it was spotless, she always felt an emptiness in her heart.","Xiaodie stared blankly into the distance for a moment before gathering her emotions. She then ran back to the side room, took out the \"Biography of the Marquis’s Mansion’s Second Son-in-Law,\" and began to write, stroke by stroke.","\"On the twenty-ninth of September in the 21st year of Anhe, Sir was reading in the study during the morning. I ran over to tell him that the Holy Emperor’s decree had arrived...\"","Naturally, Chen Yi was unaware of Xiaodie’s thoughts. He led Pei Guanli all the way through the middle courtyard and arrived at the front courtyard. At this time, Feng Erbao and the others who had come to announce the decree had just left the Xiao Family, and Elder Master Xiao and the rest were returning from the entrance.","Chen Yi ran into them head-on and bowed in greeting. \"Elder Master.\"","Elder Master Xiao’s expression was relatively relaxed, seemingly unaffected by the Holy Emperor’s decree of punishment. He glanced at Pei Guanli before his clear eyes landed on Chen Yi. He nodded with a peaceful expression and asked, \"I heard Qingzhou is going to participate in the Annual Examination tomorrow?\"","Chen Yi caught sight of Xiao Xuanshuo, Xiao Shen, and the others from the corner of his eye and responded with a smile, \"Yes.\"","\"I believe that with your knowledge, the Annual Examination won’t stump you, but don’t drop your guard either.\"","Elder Master Xiao offered a few words of encouragement. He then cheerfully greeted Pei Guanli, asked a bit about the Mountain Race’s recent situation, and led his people back to the Qingjing Residence.","Chen Yi exchanged greetings with the others one by one. Only after watching their figures disappear around the corner did he take Pei Guanli by the hand and walk out of the Marquis’s Mansion.","Pei Guanli asked thoughtfully, \"Brother-in-law, I feel like Grandpa Xiao is a bit different from before.\"","While observing the passing commoners and Wandering Martial Artists along the street, Chen Yi asked casually, \"How so?\"","\"He isn’t coughing as much? I remember when we first came to Shu State, Grandpa Xiao was terribly ill. Now, he looks as if he’s fully recovered. Furthermore...\" Pei Guanli patted her chest, causing her Bell to ring JINGLE JINGLE. \"Xiaohua says Grandpa Xiao is very formidable.\"","Chen Yi replied noncommittally, \"Is that so? Perhaps the Elder Master found a Divine Doctor.\"","\"A Divine Doctor? Brother-in-law, aren’t you...\"","\"Hmm?\"","Pei Guanli almost let the secret slip. She stuck out her tongue and shut her mouth. However, before they had taken more than a few steps, she couldn’t help but ask again, \"Brother-in-law, when do you plan to let Sister Jinghong know?\"","Chen Yi paused his steps for a brief moment before resuming his calm pace forward. \"She’ll know when it’s time for her to know.\"","\"When is that?\"","\"Take a guess...\"","Now that Liu Hong was dead, along with the vast majority of those harboring malicious intentions, the crisis facing the Xiao Family was temporarily resolved. Yet, Chen Yi still hadn’t considered revealing everything to Xiao Jinghong.","Originally, he had worried that the \"Fledgling\" identity forced onto him by the White Tiger Guard would make Xiao Jinghong suspect him of plotting against the Xiao Family. But after experiencing so many things, he suddenly realized that hiding a few secrets carried quite a few benefits.","For one, outsiders targeting the Xiao Family would largely ignore a scholar like him, at most assuming he was a frail intellectual with decent handwriting. Secondly, the Xiao Family had too few hidden trump cards, leaving them completely exposed and easily seen through by others. However, with him acting from the shadows, anyone wanting to target the Xiao Family would have to think twice.","At the very least, he needed to wait until he had cleared everything up and laid low for a while before saying anything.","***","Meanwhile, inside the Qingjing Residence.","Elder Master Xiao gave Xiao Xuanshuo, Xiao Shen, and the others a few instructions before dismissing them. The Holy Emperor’s punishment had not exceeded his expectations. But he hadn’t anticipated that the Holy Emperor would let them off so lightly this time, merely deducting three years of salary and letting the matter drop.","This actually made him somewhat worried.","After pondering for a moment, Elder Master Xiao looked towards a corner and said in a deep voice, \"Send an eagle message to Jinghong. Tell her that Feng Erbao has already visited, everything in the manor is normal, and she should focus on inspecting the troops in the Three Towns.\"","Xiao Jing agreed in a low voice. Just as he was about to leave, he heard the Elder Master continue, \"And also Chen Qingzhou...\" He hesitated for a moment before saying, \"Tell Jinghong that Qingzhou is going to take his Annual Examination tomorrow.\"","Xiao Jing agreed once more, though he inwardly disapproved. He thought that a trivial matter like the Annual Examination shouldn’t be reported to Xiao Jinghong at this time, lest it distract her.","Elder Master Xiao naturally paid no mind to Xiao Jing’s thoughts. He remained silent for a moment before ordering, \"Recently, many Wandering Martial Artists have been appearing in Shu State City. To prevent any Evil Demonic Dao among them from causing trouble, send a few people to follow Qingzhou...\" Before he could finish, he realized it was inappropriate and waved it off. \"Forget it. You go personally.\"","Xiao Jing revealed his figure in confusion. \"Marquis, you want me to protect the second son-in-law?\"","\"Protect?\" A somewhat complicated expression appeared on Elder Master Xiao’s face. \"It would be great if you could actually protect him. I’m just afraid...\" He paused mid-sentence and waved his hand. \"Just do as I say, and remember not to draw any attention.\"","Xiao Jing nodded. \"Understood.\"","Unexpectedly, Elder Master Xiao followed up with a reminder: \"Also, remember not to get too close to him. Keep a distance of at least five miles.\"","Xiao Jing was stunned and looked at him in bewilderment. \"This...\"","\"Just do it!\"","\"Yes, sir...\"","After the utterly baffled Xiao Jing left, Elder Master Xiao looked at the teacup on the table and sighed softly.","These past few days, he had been secretly investigating, mostly focusing on what Chen Yi had done and where he had gone since arriving in Shu State. Despite all his searching, he still couldn’t bring himself to believe that Chen Yi was the \"Dragon Tiger\" Liu Wu.","Although there were a few clues—such as Wang Ji practically being driven out of the Xiao Family by Chen Yi’s own hands, Chen Yi frequently visiting the Hundred Herbs Hall, or the fact that he, Chen Yu, and Liu Wu had never appeared at the same time—these were only speculations. They couldn’t definitively prove that Chen Yi was Chen Yu, or that he was the \"Dragon Tiger\" Liu Wu.","No matter how unparalleled a person’s talent was, it was impossible for them to achieve greatness across the Martial Arts, Medical Dao, and Calligraphy Dao all at once, right? Not to mention, with Chen Yu managing the Hundred Herbs Hall, Liu Wu secretly assisting the Xiao Family, and Chen Yi working as an Instructor at Guiyun Academy... he would be stretched too thin, wouldn’t he?","Elder Master Xiao rubbed his brow and thought, \"If I still don’t find anything, I’ll just have to make a move personally...\""]},{"number":605,"title":"Chapter 605 - 340: Truly a Peerless Talent","paragraphs":["Although Elder Master Xiao didn’t believe Liu Hong’s nonsense, the matter involved the internal affairs of the Xiao Family, so he had to investigate it thoroughly. This would prevent him from making any misjudgments in the future.","Just as he was thinking about this, his ears twitched slightly. A familiar voice rang out from outside the front gates.","\"Go report immediately! Tell that old thief Xiao Yuan to prepare some good wine and food. I’ve been starving for a decent meal on this damn journey!\"","\"Lord... Lord Duke? Quick, please come in first. I’ll go inform the master right away.\"","\"Come in? The main gates aren’t even open, and that old bastard Xiao hasn’t come out to greet me. What kind of manners is it for me to just walk in like this? I traveled all this way to bail your master out of trouble, so shouldn’t he come out to welcome me personally?\"","\"Yes, right away...\"","Lu Guan, who was guarding the gates, didn’t dare delay and ran inside in a panic. Hearing Duke Qian Zhang Xuan’s shameless remarks, a smile bloomed on Elder Master Xiao’s face, dispelling the annoyance caused by the Holy Emperor’s recent punishment. Before Lu Guan could reach him, he leaned on his cane and walked out of the Qingjing Residence, instructing the Personal Guard Armored Warriors along the way to prepare their finest wines and rarest delicacies.","Spotting him from a distance, Lu Guan stopped and bowed. Only when Elder Master Xiao drew near did he whisper, \"Master, Lord Duke Qian is at the gates. There are two others accompanying him...\"","Elder Master Xiao gave a hum of acknowledgment. Leaning on his cane, he strode swiftly out of the mansion gates and saw Zhang Xuan standing with his hands behind his back, facing away from him.","\"Old fool, what do you see staring up at the sky like that? Is it going to be windy or rainy tomorrow?\"","Hearing Elder Master Xiao’s teasing, Zhang Xuan turned his head. \"It’s going to hail and crush you to death, you old bastard.","\"I traveled countless miles, personally bringing men to deliver food and silver coins to you, and this is how you treat your benefactor?\"","Elder Master Xiao looked him up and down. Seeing his slightly haggard complexion, he felt a sense of gratitude and comfort, but his words remained unforgiving. \"During the great battle five years ago, when Left King Mu Hage charged the lines, you almost died under his Heavy Mace. Who blocked it for you?","\"And twenty years ago, who led three thousand soldiers of the Profound Armor Army to arrive just in time to save you?\"","Seeing him bringing up the past again, Zhang Xuan waved his hand repeatedly. \"Alright, alright! That was years ago, why even bring it up?\" He pointed at the gates of the Marquis’s Mansion. \"Is this your way of treating guests?\"","Knowing Zhang Xuan was acting shamelessly just to find a way out of the argument, Elder Master Xiao waved his hand, signaling Lu Guan to open the main gates. \"Let’s go drink.\"","\"That’s more like it.\"","Zhang Xuan walked past Elder Master Xiao with his head held high, not forgetting to instruct the two men behind him, \"Wait outside the city. I’ll have someone notify you later about where to deliver the grain.\"","\"Yes, Lord Duke.\" The two middle-aged men, dressed in green robes with long blades hanging from their waists, cupped their hands in a salute before turning and riding away.","Elder Master Xiao glanced at the two men and caught up with Zhang Xuan. \"Their Cultivation is not weak.\"","Zhang Xuan kept his head held high and said proudly, \"Of course the experts my son found aren’t weak. Did you think everyone is like you, guarding against Jianghu People like they’re thieves?\"","Elder Master Xiao ignored the tease and asked thoughtfully, \"You weren’t this cautious the last time you visited... Did something happen?\"","Zhang Xuan paused, his chin lowering as his expression darkened. \"Those people have been getting more and more rampant lately.\"","\"Who? Those bandits on the eastern sea?\"","\"Who else would dare to pillage my Guangyue Prefecture? If it weren’t for a traitor inside tipping them off, I would have led my troops to wipe them out long ago!\"","Elder Master Xiao frowned slightly. \"Treason?\"","Zhang Xuan snorted. \"Just a bunch of greedy opportunists. Unrefined scum.\"","\"If they’re truly just unrefined scum, why did you bring two experts along?\"","\"You... My son is filial and worried about his old man. Is that a crime?\"","Seeing Zhang Xuan being stubborn to the bitter end, Elder Master Xiao shook his head. \"Traitors from within are more dangerous than enemies from without. It’s good to take precautions.\"","Zhang Xuan waved a hand dismissively. \"Let’s not talk about such depressing matters. I heard you killed Liu Gongmo and were punished by a decree from the Holy Emperor. Tell me, did Liu Gongmo really commit those heinous acts?\"","Elder Master Xiao nodded slightly. \"More than that. He colluded deeply with both the Barbarian Race and the Poshisu Country.\" He paused, his expression turning sorrowful. \"Fengchun’s whereabouts were discovered by the Barbarian Race because he secretly tipped them off.\"","\"Him?!\" Zhang Xuan immediately cursed him as a dog. \"To think Fengchun once saved his life! How dare he bite the hand that fed him?","\"That scum, that bastard, that ungrateful wretch... Old Xiao, you really shouldn’t have let him die so easily. People like him deserve death by a thousand cuts!","\"Why did you kill him so early, and even get yourself punished by the Holy Emperor? You let that dog off too easily!\"","Elder Master Xiao smiled bitterly and shook his head, offering no response.","If Liu Hong hadn’t been dead set on seeking his own demise by bringing up Fu Wanqing, Elder Master Xiao wouldn’t have killed him, no matter how furious he was. But thinking about it now, it was better that he had. If Liu Hong had gone to the Capital Prefecture alive and revealed that Fu Wanqing was among the Barbarian Race, the consequences would have been far more unacceptable. Elder Master Xiao didn’t dare to imagine how Xiao Jinghong would react if he found out.","Unaware of all this, Zhang Xuan cursed for a while before pulling him along, declaring that they wouldn’t stop drinking until they were thoroughly drunk tonight. Naturally, Elder Master Xiao didn’t object.","As soon as they took their seats, Zhang Xuan looked at him, the anger freezing on his face. He pointed at him and asked, \"Wait, Old Xiao, you... your health... are you cured?\"","As he instructed the servants to bring the wine and food, Elder Master Xiao smiled and nodded. \"I’m doing a bit better.\"","\"Just a bit better? Looking at your physique, I’d say your old injuries are completely healed!\" Seeing his friend smile without saying a word, Zhang Xuan’s face darkened. \"You’re still hiding things from me? Tell me, who has such incredible ability?\"","\"It’s...\"","Elder Master Xiao thought of Chen Yu and Liu Wu, and then Chen Yi’s face surfaced in his mind. The words reached the tip of his tongue, but he swallowed them back, merely shaking his head as he said..."]}]);
